      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Two things stopped me.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended amlodipine dose for adults is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile justifies a higher dose. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient. Please ask the patient's treating physician or another authorized prescriber to confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, send it to me and I can enter it. If they intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves and document why. Pharmacy would also need to verify it."
      }
